{"diagnosis": "Loopback send of 0xa5 was received as 0xe9, triggering FAIL 0xdead uart data mismatch trap. 0xa5=10100101 shifted by one data bit yields 0xe9=11101001, consistent with no start-bit falling edge. Root cause is line 126 loading send_pattern as {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b1} with LSB=1 (idle) instead of 1'b0 (start), so the receiver aligns on the next zero.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@
 			end else
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
-				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b1};
+				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b0};
 				send_bitcnt <= 10;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else", "expected": "tohost: PASS, uart data match got 0xa5 want 0xa5, TRAP cleared"}

